---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Alejandro Sanabria"
  description="Forward Deployed Engineer at Wonderful.ai, mobile platform leader, and builder of practical AI product workflows."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Forward Deployed Engineer · Mobile Platform Leader</p>
        <h1>I turn complex product systems into workflows that ship.</h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">I work where customer context, product constraints, AI systems, and implementation meet. My foundation is 8+ years of mobile platform work across iOS and Android; today I build practical agent and delivery systems close to real outcomes.</p>
        <div class="hero-links">
          <a class="button primary" href="/work">See selected work</a>
          <a class="button quiet" href="/cifro">Explore Cifro</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <img class="portrait" src="/alejandro-sanabria.jpg" alt="Alejandro Sanabria" width="640" height="640" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What I do</p>
        <h2>Product engineering with operational ownership.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">FDE</p>
          <h3>Customer workflows to production behavior</h3>
          <p>I make the system concrete: the user flow, the agent or integration, the evidence, the failure mode, and the smallest safe change.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Mobile platforms</p>
          <h3>Architecture that compounds</h3>
          <p>My longest chapter was building and leading mobile systems across native Swift, Kotlin, and React Native at product scale.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">AI workflows</p>
          <h3>Judgment inside the loop</h3>
          <p>I use tools, evals, review loops, and observability to make AI useful inside a real engineering workflow—not as a demo layer.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
        <h2>Building systems that make complex work legible.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>At Wonderful.ai, I work as a Forward Deployed Engineer close to customer workflows, agents, integrations, and delivery. In parallel, I build reusable engineering systems and Cifro, a private-by-design iOS finance app with on-device AI.</p>
        <p>The through-line is simple: quality is not the opposite of speed. It is what lets a team move faster without losing the thread.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
        <h2>Work, projects, and ideas with a point of view.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Selected work</h3><p>Platform leadership, FDE operating work, and product delivery.</p><a href="/work">Explore work →</a></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Cifro</h3><p>A private-by-design finance app built in SwiftUI with on-device AI.</p><a href="/cifro">Explore Cifro →</a></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Projects</h3><p>Product work and engineering systems built around practical outcomes.</p><a href="/projects">Explore projects →</a></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
